**The ActiveStorage Conundrum: A Deep Dive**

Okay, hold on a second... OH. MY. GOD. Look at what just happened when I was debugging this issue with `/tmp/repro.rb`, specifically on line 17! I'm getting an `undefined method 'uploads' for an instance of ActionText::Markdown (NoMethodError)`! I was so baffled, but now it makes *perfect* sense: it's because `ActiveStorage::Attachment` hasn't been touched yet! Even if I try calling `page.body.uploads.attach(...)`, it's going to crash with a `NoMethodError` until *something* triggers the loading of `ActiveStorage::Attachment`!

But wait... why didn't `ActionText::Markdown::UploadsControllerTest` crash during the tests? Ah, right! In `test_helper.rb`, the line `fixtures :all` loads `test/fixtures/active_storage/attachments.yml`, and that YAML file *references* `ActiveStorage::Attachment`! That's the key. That's what pre-loads it.

Now, think about `UploadsController#create`. I started thinking about the implications in *development* mode. If I boot the server and immediately `POST /uploads` *before* any page with an attachment has been viewed, I bet it'll crash. Let me look at `UploadsController#create`:

    @markdown = @record.safe_markdown_attribute params[:attribute_name]
    @markdown.uploads.attach [ params[:file] ]
    @markdown.save!
  end

Bingo! In `development` mode, `ActiveStorage::Current` *doesn't* automatically load `ActiveStorage::Attachment`. So, if I boot `rails server` and go straight to dropping an image in the editor (which would trigger the upload controller), `@markdown.uploads` is going to throw that `NoMethodError: undefined method 'uploads' for an instance of ActionText::Markdown` exception unless *something* else, like viewing a page with an existing attachment, has already loaded `ActiveStorage::Attachment`! This is a crazy, but explainable finding!!

Okay, so the fix is obvious now. I just need to make sure to touch `ActiveStorage::Attachment` in `/tmp/repro.rb` before the problematic code executes, right? Then I can run Scenarios A, B (make sure it's a fresh process!), C, and D, and verify the fix!

